%erg 0.1
Title: Add a gofmt + go vet adherence ratchet to the test suite
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T03:35Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

git-erg has no mechanical Go-formatting/vet gate -- the analog of the Python
ruff adherence check the harness rules mandate. `make check` runs the suite +
corpus validation but never `gofmt -l` or `go vet`, so formatting drift only
gets caught by a human reviewer or /verify's ad-hoc pass. The /verify on PR
#242 (ticket 0207) flagged this gap directly, and pre-existing gofmt drift has
been observed in version.go / ref_test.go / refs_test.go.

CAUTION (machine-specific): on padme the local `gofmt -w` corrupts the ASCII
`'\''` in src/go/version.go's shellSingleQuote comment into a UTF-8 curly
quote (`gofmt -d` confirms gofmt itself wants the change -- a broken local
gofmt/proxy). A ratchet that runs `gofmt -l` is fine (read-only); a fixer that
runs `gofmt -w` must not be wired into any automated path until that is
understood. See the memory note. CI's real gofmt is byte-faithful.

## Actions

1. Add `tests/test_gofmt.sh`: assert `gofmt -l src/go/` prints nothing
   (read-only; no `-w`), and `cd src/go && go vet ./...` exits 0. Register the
   suite in the Makefile TEST_SUITES.
2. Fix any pre-existing drift the ratchet surfaces (version.go, ref_test.go,
   refs_test.go, ...) -- by hand or with a REAL gofmt, never the broken local
   `gofmt -w` on version.go (verify line 59 stays `'\''`, ASCII).

## Test

`tests/test_gofmt.sh` with a negative control (a deliberately mis-indented
temp .go file is reported by `gofmt -l`), so the ratchet is non-vacuous.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `tests/test_gofmt.sh` exists, registered in TEST_SUITES.
- [ ] `gofmt -l src/go/` is clean (drift fixed by hand / real gofmt).
- [ ] `go vet ./...` clean.
- [ ] Negative control proves the check fails on injected drift.
- [ ] `make check` passes; src/go stays pure ASCII (version.go:59 intact).
